      "id": 1,
      "text": "Mullen was named after railroad official Charles Mullen and was laid out in 1888 when the Burlington railroad extended to the area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mullen%2C_Nebraska"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Hooker County was established in 1889, and Mullen became its county seat, making it the only settlement in the county at that time.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://mynehistory.com/items/show/283"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The first courthouse in Hooker County was completed in 1889, right after Mullen was designated the county seat.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mullen%2C_Nebraska"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Mullen was incorporated as a village in 1907, solidifying its status in the Nebraska Sandhills.",
